                               IMPORTANT NOTES
      
         There are a couple very important notes that must be 
         mentioned before we get into this doc. They concern 
         successful completion of Falcon missions and campaigns.
      
         First, when you fly a mission in Falcon, at least one F-16 
         must survive or the mission will be a failure. This means if 
         your wingmen pilot aircraft other than F-16s, and you're in 
         the *ONLY* F-16, you'd better survive the mission. If you 
         don't, it's either abort or fail!
      
         Second, when you're closing in on victory in a campaign, 
         don't move your home base right up to the front (and if it is 
         there, move it back a little--you should have at least one 
         friendly site as a buffer).  Falcon has a tendency to get 
         confused and hang up if it has to move your home base *and* 
         declare victory at the start of the same 0600 mission.  (You'll 
         recognize the problem: first you'll get the announcement that 
         your base is being moved, and then Falcon will hang.) If it 


                                                                          


      Strategic FALCON            Version 1.1 Update                Page 3
      --------------------------------------------------------------------

         happens, run RESTRCAM and create a buffer site manually 
         before reflying the 2300 hr mission.
      
      
