                                 Kill Boxes:
      
      Q. About Kill Boxes--does a second F-16 flight in a different 
         box need to have the point of view focused on it to wake up 
         the ambient ground forces?
      
      A. Yes. The big point is this: only one kill box is active at a 
         time--and that's the one where *you* are. If the second F-16 
         flight is out of your kill box, the ground forces there are 
         inactive. When you jump to that wingman view, though, they wake 
         up--often right underneath the flight. (This surprises the hell 
         out of those pilots!) That's why you have to watch the other 
         flight "all the way in" from about 7 miles out: they'll have 
         time to properly set up attacks that way.
      
      Q. If Falcon 3.0 creates enemy ground forces, are they active 
         independent of point of view?
      
      A. Yes, they're active all the time. Kill boxes only apply to 
         the units at a *site*.
      
      

                                                                          


