      --------------------------------------------------------------------

         flights (who have not set up any attacks on them, because 
         they're "off" when you're not there!) and toast your planes.
         
         First, make sure you start the mission with the ground attack 
         (StratFalc flights) *at least* 7-10 miles from their target, 
         and when they get to about that point, set your autopilot and 
         jump to the wingman view of the StratFalc flight that is 
         closest. 
         
         Also, if the site is close to the edge of a kill box, make 
         sure you're not coming in over that edge.  If the aircraft 
         are too close to the SAMs when they wake up, the planes 
         won't have time to set up attacks.
         
         These are the keys:
         
         * Give your SF aircraft plenty of room to set up.
         
         * Make sure they don't come at a site that's close to the edge 
           of a kill box from over that near edge (try to get at 
           least 7 miles).
         
         * Once the ground strike craft get close to the site (within 
           about 7-10 miles), watch the attack all the way in.
         
         * If you can't watch the site all the way in with the wingman 
           view (as you know, sometimes StratFalc flights go "out of 
           range"), use the Transporter Room method described on  Page 21 
           of the manual to activate the site and keep it activated until 
           your attack can hit it.
         
